From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:00:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] accel/ane: keep an idle H16 engine powered by default

With no program loaded, the H16 engine powers off h16_idle_off_ms after
its firmware first runs. On the J604 that first power-off lands about
5.3 s into boot, inside the window where some boots still stop before
the watchdog resets them, next to the external display power-down and
the speaker start.

Make 0 the default, so the engine stays powered from bring-up, and
leave the idle power-off one module parameter away. The power-off with
programs loaded (h16_idle_off_loaded_ms) only runs after a request, so
it stays as it is. System sleep keeps its own power-off.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_backend.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_backend.c b/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_backend.c
index ecad2f4017..b7f01243a2 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_backend.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_backend.c
@@ -673,10 +673,14 @@ static void ane_h16_sleep_resume(struct ane_h16_device *h)
  * on the engine booted again from the preload, as after a cold system
  * sleep. 0 keeps the engine powered while any program is loaded.
  */
-static unsigned int h16_idle_off_ms = 1000;
+/*
+ * Off by default for now: the first idle power-off lands about 5.3 s into
+ * boot, inside the window where some J604 boots still stop.
+ */
+static unsigned int h16_idle_off_ms;
 module_param(h16_idle_off_ms, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(h16_idle_off_ms,
-		 "Power the H16 ANE off after this many idle ms with no program loaded (0: keep it powered; default: 1000)");
+		 "Power the H16 ANE off after this many idle ms with no program loaded (default 0: keep it powered)");
 
 static unsigned int h16_idle_off_loaded_ms = 5000;
 module_param(h16_idle_off_loaded_ms, uint, 0644);
-- 
2.43.0

